		(uuid "230559a0-682e-5030-9e80-fe8bf70f5c82")
	)
	(text "U201 LMR36510ADDA, 400 kHz, SNVSBD7B Table 8-1 (5 V row): L 22 uH, COUT 2 x 22 uF, RFBT 100k, RFBB 24.9k,\n  CIN 2.2 uF + 220 nF; here C201 4.7u 50 V X7R + C202 220n 50 V. VOUT = 1.0 V x (1 + 100k/24.9k) = 5.02 V (Eq. 3).\n  VIN abs max 70 V, recommended 65 V: above VC 53.3 V of D101. CBOOT 100n >= 16 V (§8.2.1.2.6); VCC 1u (§8.2.1.2.7).\n  EN UVLO (Eq. 10): VON = 1.231 V x (1 + 100k/20k) = 7.4 V, VOFF = 7.4 x (1 - 0.110/1.231) = 6.7 V (HW-PWR-004).\n  Ripple (Eq. 4): (24 - 5)/(400k x 22u) x 5/24 = 0.45 A pp (45 % of 1 A); LMIN = 0.625 x 5/400k = 7.8 uH (Eq. 5).\n  L201 Isat must be >= ILIMIT 1.6 A max (§8.2.1.2.3): not read from the Sunlord datasheet, open item OI-3.\n  C205/C206 are 6.3 V X5R at 5 V: effective capacitance under DC bias is an ASSUMPTION (OI-4).\nD201/D202 SS34 (40 V, 3 A) OR 5V_BUCK and VBUS: each blocks back-feed into the other source (HW-PWR-005).\nU202 AP2112K-3.3: 600 mA, dropout 250 mV typ at 600 mA; CIN = COUT = 1 uF ceramic (Diodes AP2112 datasheet).\n  +5V >= 4.5 V after the Schottky, so >= 1 V headroom. P = (4.6 - 3.3) V x 0.15 A = 0.2 W at the expected load.\nC209 4.7u is the +5V bulk; VBUS capacitance seen by the host stays C601 only (D202 blocks C209)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 91.44 127 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "2e0e72ed-68fa-5ab4-b033-03439adb7969")
	)
